Erm, i strongly suspect that the amount of RAM is not quite right - i
wouldn't think that you could run Win98 with less than 16MB. Can it be
that the OS is behaving strangely? NetHack is so light on processor
power that you'd need to use something like a 10MHz machine to make it
notably slow, i would think (now ADOM is a whole different matter -
100MHz are probably the slowest sort of machine you can run it on
without serious damage to your mental equilibrium).

I've played NetHack 3.2.x on a 25MHz computer with possibly 8MB, but
i'm not sure DOS was configured well enough to really use all that
memory. Ran perfectly smoothly, anyway. 

> BTW, is there a way to protect against disease?

Polymorph into a violet fungus ;)
The on average safest way of course is to just whack away at Juiblex
and get rid of disease whenever you're made ill (and the cheapest
method of becoming un-sick is the application of a unicorn, preferably
blessed; but it's not fail-safe). If you know the workings of deadly
illness, you can even afford killing Juiblex and remove sickness
_then_.

I do remember that we had some enormous trouble finding out how to
handle Juiblex when we were busy learning the game (with outmoded
spoilers and lots of savefile cheating); we only knew that prayers
could remove sickness, and since Juiblex is most often encountered in
Gehennom, this made things rather difficult. It was quite a bit later
that we found out about unicorn horns ...

